<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/5th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty · Peace</p><h1 class="enc-title">Treaty of Nvarsak</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">484</span> · <a href="/centuries/5th-century">5th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Treaty of Nvarsak was concluded in 484 between the Armenian leader Vahan Mamikonian and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sasanian-empire">Sasanian Empire</a> after years of Armenian revolt. It granted the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/armenians">Armenians</a> freedom to practise <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christianity">Christianity</a>, removed Zoroastrian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fire-temple">fire temples</a> from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/armenia">Armenia</a> and allowed the nobility to govern their lands, and Vahan was later appointed marzpan. It secured the religious toleration that the rising of 451 had fought for.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/treaty-of-nvarsak.jpg" alt="Treaty of Nvarsak" width="320" height="266" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Julian Zasso · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_return_to_the_homeland.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
